operations=Add promote: only the installed binary may judge. It pins the gate, runs it in the checkout, exercises the candidate with seed, reject and extend checks of its own, keeps candidate and predecessor in the job folder, replaces itself and writes the record. A running service that finds its binary replaced exits before the next job so that the supervisor starts the successor.
checks=PASS: Rust tests including promotion by the installed binary, a refused foreign judge, a pinned gate, a failing gate, a hollow candidate and the service handover. Clippy, release build, service restart.
